? Which tool moves the viewed region without moving the object?
+ Pan
- Select and Move
- Face Extrude
- Lathe
= Pan changes the view.

? Which source viewport is normally a perspective view?
+ Perspective
- Top
- Front
- Left
= The other named default views are orthographic.

? What makes a primitive parametric?
+ Editable settings update geometry
- Every face is a photograph
- Every object is permanently fixed
- All material maps are deleted
= Parameters retain controllable construction values.

? Which operation makes repeated regular rows of objects?
+ Array
- Zoom
- Crop
- Audio mix
= An array systematically repeats selected objects.

? What does Snapshot clone from an animated object?
+ States sampled along its motion
- Only the first material name
- Only the viewport grid colour
- Only the keyboard shortcut list
= Snapshot can sample time or distance along motion.

? Why keep a primitive copy before conversion?
+ Original parameters may be lost
- Conversion always deletes the scene
- All textures must become audio
- No other object can be created
= Editable conversion may remove parametric construction access.

? Which method revolves a profile around an axis?
+ Lathe
- Extrude
- Pan
- Mirror
= Lathe suits rotational forms such as the pawn.

? What does Extrude add to a flat shape?
+ Depth
- Frame rate
- Sound
- Font mapping
= Extrusion extends geometry into another dimension.

? What does a Loft require?
+ A path and cross-sections
- Only a sound and its duration
- Only an empty camera view
- Only a finished render file
= Cross-sections are arranged along the path.

? What does Auto Key record when used correctly?
+ Parameter values at chosen frames
- Every possible hardware setting
- Only the screen brightness value
- Only the final output filename
= Changes at frames become keys for interpolation.

? What does texture mapping chiefly add?
+ Surface appearance detail
- Automatic silhouette geometry
- A compulsory camera movement
- An extra physical display
= Images supply detail without modelling each feature.

? Which inputs contribute to a rendered image?
+ Geometry, materials, lights and view
- Only the source file name
- Only the count of menu items
- Only the keyboard layout
= Rendering calculates the scene from the selected view.
